==Battleground==
*5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*2 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal One Horn]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is one of the most feared stages from Growing Strange by many players, due to being a metal stage, clearing it can be incredibly inconsistent. Using [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] that can easily stall [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] foes ([[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Poseidon]] can almost perma-[[Freeze|freeze]] if you stack two and time them correctly; [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaguya]] and [[Mitama the Oracle|Mitama]] are also amazing), and slowly kill the enemies using some [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critical hitters]]. With this approach, all you really need are meatshields and any critical hitter as support.

Don't waste space on meatshields and only bring one very strong [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]], hoping for RNG and spamming everything your money allows you to spam as meatshields, even units that aren't normally used for this if you have plenty of money.

Using consistent anti-Metal [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd control]] (preferably [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster & Charley]], [[Talents|talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]], or some Uber Rare) and try to stack at least 5 [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cats]] at the start and then just spam meatshields and other units for protection afterwards.

